bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_f64_option_unwrap_or_expect_try_readers_lossy_2026-11-27, 0, "Typed f64? readers NOT covered by the rt_option_float_bits fix (seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27); same result on the base seed, found in review. (1) val c: f64? = Some(0.1); c.unwrap_or(9.0) lowers through rt_unwrap_or_value, which decodes the explicit Some payload as a legacy inline float and drops the low 3 mantissa bits (0.09999999999999998). (2) c.expect(\"m\") == 0.1 and a struct field h.a.expect(..) == 0.1 are false even though the payload bits are exact: the expect path does not route through the float-option reader. (3) val v = c? (try operator inside an fn returning an optional) binds the lossy value. Fix direction: route rt_unwrap_or_value / expect / try over a float optional through mir read_present_float_option_payload (lowering_core.rs) the same way the rt_unwrap_or_self float arm does. (4) Related runtime residual: when the heap-float allocation fails, rt_value_float falls back to the legacy inline TAG_FLOAT form (payload << 3), so the low 3 bits come back as 010 regardless of reader; a typed f64? needs a tag separate from the payload (seed_typed_f64_option_some_heap_allocates_per_some_never_released_2026-11-27)."
    seed_jit_f64_option_unwrap_or_expect_try_readers_lossy_2026-11-27, 1, "FIX IMPLEMENTED 2026-11-27 (work/f64-option-inline-layout-20261127, mir/float_option_inline.rs): typed f64? locals carry a real tag separate from the payload, so (1) c.unwrap_or(d) on a typed local with a literal or local default is lowered in HIR as a typed coalesce (exact, no runtime call, no box; base grew 552 MB over 2e7 calls), (2) .expect(m) reads the exact bits (it already did on the base seed for a typed local; pinned by the spec), (3) val v = c? binds an exactly boxed float when HIR left v erased, and the nil-word denormal (bits == 3) is present for ??, if val, match, unwrap_or and ? because presence is the tag alone. Red to green on aarch64: fixture readers 27 mismatches on base seed dc41771399af764f, 0 on fix seed dd4adb4888424f68; carriers fixture nilword 872257 to 0. Not changed: (4) the rt_value_float allocation-failure fallback to the lossy inline form, and unwrap_or receivers that are not a plain typed local (mk(x).unwrap_or(d), h.a.unwrap_or(d)) or whose default is not a literal or local still take the lossy dynamic rt_unwrap_or_value; the ? payload bound to an erased slot costs one boxed float per ?."

